<td><!-- #BeginEditable "cardstrategy" -->
<p>
<b>Dagobah</b><br>
From Gregg Keefer, Gold 4 <br><br>
 This is by far one of the best choices for a starting loccation you can 
use
for the Light Side as it gives HUGE Force generation in a hurry! You'll
activate 2 Force (plus 1 for yourself) on your first turn and there is a
tradeoff as it gives the same amount to your opponent but the card text of
this location allows you to make this up every turn if you put additional
Dagobah sites in your deck. During your deploy phase you may dig out any
Dagobah site from your Reserve Deck and deploy it! This saves you the 
trouble
of waiting to draw up sites to get the Force flowing. I only put one such 
site
in my deck and that is Yoda's Hut (2 Force for me and zip for them), on my
first turn I deploy it and BAM, on my second turn I am activating 5 
Force. <br><br>All
the Dagobah sites are good for you and do nothing for your opponent but 
too
many of them will restrict your Force drain options so I usually only put 
in
one or two to get the Force flowing and then move on to my real strategy.
These sites will keep your opponent off balance, thinking you are playing 
a
Dagobah drain or Jedi Training deck when you are really going to Cloud 
City or
Tatooine.
 <br><br> In addition to the Force generation, having these sites on the table 
lets
you play Stone Piles and take 2 cards at random from your opponent's hand 
and
place them in limbo on Dagobah. There is nothing sweeter than a lucky pick
removing the Executor or some other vital card from their strategy early 
in
the game!
  So come back to Dagobah. It's a slimy mudhole.

<br><br><br>
<b>Dagobah</b><br>
From <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20040810091421/mailto:nicai@singnet.com.sg">Nicholas Cai</a> <br><br>

Nobody would have thought a location like this could help you win the 
game! It sort of works like this: use Dagobah's "search" ability and 
deploy a Dagobah location every turn. This guarantees you Force every 
turn! Use the extra Force to deploy characters, and this also gives you 
complete card drawing advantage! It works well with any deck. Best of 
all, Yoda would have a place to deploy to (at his hut, he subtracts 2 
from attrition!) . The possibilities are just endless.



</p>
